       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release, given as no more than about 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 to 2,550 mg per day.\n- **Risk:** At 5,100 mg per day, the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a mix-up between the per-dose and daily totals. Some possible intended orders:\n\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, such as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason. I would still suggest a pharmacist or attending review before I enter it."
