     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem, and I can't verify the clinical rationale from here.\n\n1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. That's about twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg, and each dose is well above the usual 850 to 1,000 mg ceiling. I don't know of any indication or stage of treatment that calls for this dose. The main risks are metformin-associated lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Examples are 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals. I can enter either right away.\n- **Get a pharmacist or attending to review it.** If an exception is truly warranted, they can approve it and document the rationale. Your institution's process for out-of-range doses should handle that, and it will likely require an override that I can't do for you.\n- **Check the source of the dose.** Compare it against the original plan or consult note. It may be a transcription error, for example 1,700 mg as a daily total.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter one of the in-range options."
      }
     ],
